  {
   "id": "bava_batra.78a.3",
   "daf": "78a",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ הַמּוֹכֵר אֶת הַחֲמוֹר – לֹא מָכַר כֵּלָיו. נַחוּם הַמָּדִי אוֹמֵר: מָכַר כֵּלָיו. רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: פְּעָמִים מְכוּרִין, פְּעָמִים אֵינָן מְכוּרִין – כֵּיצַד? הָיָה חֲמוֹר לְפָנָיו, וְכֵלָיו עָלָיו, וְאָמַר לוֹ: ״מְכוֹר לִי חֲמוֹרְךָ זֶה״ – הֲרֵי כֵּלָיו מְכוּרִין. ״חֲמוֹרְךָ הוּא״ – אֵין כֵּלָיו מְכוּרִין.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» «One who sells a donkey has not sold its vessels,» i.e., its equipment, with it. «Naḥum the Mede says:» He has «sold its vessels. Rabbi Yehuda says:» There are «times» when the vessels «are sold,» and there are «times» when «they are not sold. How so? If the donkey was before him and its vessels» were «on it, and» the buyer «said to him: Sell me this donkey of yours, its vessels are sold.» If the buyer said to him: «Is the donkey yours;» I wish to purchase it, «its vessels are not sold.»"
  }
 ],
